<div style="width: 100%; background-color: #1a5276; color: #ffffff; text-align: center; padding: 15px 0; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Checking in on Health</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Using Health Technology to Form Good Habits</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Describe dreams, hopes, and ambitions. Interactive: Discuss general habits and their impact on life.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can describe personal dreams and ambitions related to health and wellness, using clear and organized speech (e.g., "I hope to become a nutritionist so I can help people make healthier food choices.")<br>Can discuss general health habits and their impact on well-being in a conversation with peers (e.g., "Exercising regularly can improve your mood and help manage stress.")<br>Can express hypothetical ideas about achieving life balance with the help of health technology, using appropriate language structures (e.g., "If I had a sleep tracker, I would try to improve my bedtime routine.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by asking students to think about their current health <b>habits</b>. "What have you <b>been doing</b> to <b>maintain</b> your <b>health</b> and <b>well-being</b> lately?" Students briefly share in pairs. The teacher then asks, "Do you use any <b>health technology</b>, like a <b>tracker</b> or an <b>app</b>, to help you with your <b>routine</b> or to <b>monitor</b> your <b>activity level</b>?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models phrases for discussing ongoing health efforts, hypothetical improvements, and polite suggestions. For example: "I have <b>been exercising</b> daily to <b>improve</b> my <b>fitness</b>." (Emphasize /b/ in 'been', /s/ in 'exercise'). "If I had a <b>sleep tracker</b>, I <b>would try</b> to <b>boost</b> my <b>energy</b> levels." (Focus on /s/ in 'sleep', /b/ in 'boost'). "You <b>might want</b> to consider using a <b>mindfulness app</b> to <b>manage stress</b>. That sounds tough." (Modeling modal for possibility, empathy, /s/ in 'stress'). The teacher emphasizes clear articulation of health-related vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'I have been practicing meditation,' does it mean I finished practicing, or I'm still doing it as an ongoing routine?" (Expected answer: "You are still doing it, it's an ongoing effort.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If someone says, 'If I ate healthier, I might feel more energetic,' are they talking about a real event that happened, or a hypothetical situation?" (Expected answer: "A hypothetical situation, something they imagine.")</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Checking in on Health"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio dialogue (or written dialogue for teacher to read aloud) between two friends, Alex and Ben, discussing their health and how health technology helps them. The dialogue will embed the target grammar (Present perfect continuous, Second conditional, Modals for possibility) and vocabulary (e.g., <b>well-being</b>, <b>hydration</b>, <b>mindfulness</b>, <b>tracker</b>, <b>habits</b>, <b>stress</b>, <b>routine</b>, <b>improve</b>, <b>boost</b>, <b>manage</b>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example excerpt:
                <i>Alex: "Hey Ben, you look more energized these days! How have you <b>been managing</b> your <b>stress</b>?"</i>
                <i>Ben: "Thanks, Alex! I've <b>been practicing meditation</b> daily with a new <b>app</b>. It's really helped my overall <b>well-being</b>. If I hadn't started using it, I <b>would still be struggling</b> with <b>sleep patterns</b>. Also, I have <b>been tracking</b> my <b>hydration</b> with a smart water bottle."</i>
                <i>Alex: "Wow, that's great! I've <b>been trying</b> to <b>exercise</b> more, but it's tough to stay <b>consistent</b>. I <b>might need</b> some extra motivation."</i>
                <i>Ben: "You <b>could try</b> a <b>fitness tracker</b>. If you wore one, it <b>would give</b> you <b>feedback</b> on your <b>activity level</b> and remind you to move. It's an <b>essential</b> tool for building <b>regular habits</b>."</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Participates in conversations about health and well-being, exchanging information, opinions, and feelings, using appropriate language and tone.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions:</b> "What is the main topic of Alex and Ben's conversation?" and "Which health technologies do they mention?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen again and decide if statements are True or False (e.g., "Ben has been practicing meditation without any technology." - False; "Alex uses a smart water bottle to track hydration." - False).</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice using the Present perfect continuous for ongoing health efforts, the Second conditional for hypothetical well-being improvements, and Modals of possibility (<i>might, could</i>) for suggesting health strategies. They will integrate vocabulary related to <b>health</b>, <b>fitness</b>, <b>well-being</b>, <b>hydration</b>, <b>mindfulness</b>, <b>balance</b>, <b>habits</b>, <b>stress</b>, <b>tracker</b>, <b>app</b>, <b>routine</b>, <b>exercise</b>, <b>improve</b>, <b>track</b>, <b>manage</b>, <b>balanced</b>, <b>hydrated</b>, <b>healthy</b>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> Students complete sentences with the correct form of the verb (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional) or the appropriate modal verb from a given list, incorporating target vocabulary.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I _______ _______ (practice) ________ to reduce my _________." (meditation, stress)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I _______ (have) a better ________ _________, I _______ (feel) more _________." (sleep pattern, would feel, energized)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You _________ (modal of possibility) _________ (try) a _________ _________ to _________ your _________." (might, tracker app, monitor, activity level)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Substitution Drill (Pair Work):</b> In pairs, students create new sentences by substituting underlined words/phrases with options from a provided list.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence frame 1: "I have been <ins>drinking more water</ins> to improve my <ins>hydration</ins>." (Options for drinking: *exercising regularly, meditating daily*; Options for hydration: *fitness, mindfulness, energy levels*)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence frame 2: "If I <ins>had a personal nutritionist</ins>, I <ins>would achieve a healthier diet</ins>." (Options for Had: *had a smart watch, had more free time*; Options for would achieve: *would track my sleep, would join a yoga class*)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence frame 3: "You <ins>could try</ins> <ins>a sleep tracking app</ins> to <ins>monitor your sleep patterns</ins>." (Options for could try: *might need to, should consider*; Options for app: *mindfulness exercises, a fitness tracker*)</li>
                        </ul>
                        Students are encouraged to practice pronunciation of /b/ and /p/ in words like 'balance' and 'practice', and /s/ and /z/ in 'stress' and 'exercise', paying attention to sentence rhythm for PPC.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Q&A:</b> Students ask each other "What have you been doing to maintain a <b>balanced lifestyle</b>?" and "If you had a health <b>tracker</b>, how <b>would</b> you <b>improve</b> your <b>well-being</b>?" They respond using target grammar and vocabulary, providing specific examples. Teacher circulates, providing corrective feedback on grammar and pronunciation.</li>
                </ol></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Checking in on Health"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Health Check-in Role-Play.</b> Students work in pairs to perform a role-play.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student A:</b> Is a friend describing their current health <b>habits</b>, some challenges they are facing (e.g., <b>stress</b>, lack of <b>energy</b>, inconsistent <b>sleep patterns</b>), and their health <b>ambitions</b>. They must use the present perfect continuous to talk about ongoing efforts (e.g., "I have <b>been struggling</b> with motivation to <b>exercise</b>.") and express hopes (e.g., "I hope to <b>maintain</b> a more <b>balanced diet</b>.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Student B:</b> Is another friend or a "health tech enthusiast" who offers advice and shows <b>empathy</b>. They must use the second conditional to suggest hypothetical solutions with health technology (e.g., "If you used a <b>fitness tracker</b>, you <b>would get feedback</b> on your <b>activity level</b>."), and modals of possibility to give polite health <b>suggestions</b> (e.g., "You <b>might want</b> to try a <b>mindfulness app</b> to help <b>manage stress</b>."). They should also use formal expressions when making recommendations (e.g., "Could you <b>consider</b> a <b>sleep tracker</b>?").</li>
                </ul>
                Students are encouraged to incorporate a wide range of the target vocabulary (e.g., <b>well-being</b>, <b>hydration</b>, <b>nutrition</b>, <b>routine</b>, <b>self-care</b>, <b>tracker</b>, <b>app</b>, <b>reminder</b>) and focus on clear pronunciation and appropriate sentence rhythm. The teacher observes for fluency, collaborative interaction, and the successful completion of the communicative task, specifically how they convey suggestions and empathy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy: Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</b> The teacher uses a checklist to observe student performance during the role-play, focusing on the criteria below. Students also use a simplified checklist to provide feedback to their partners.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The "Health Check-in Role-Play" from Stage 4.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation of /b/ (balance, boost) vs /p/ (practice, prevent) and /s/ (stress, sleep) vs /z/ (exercise), and appropriate sentence rhythm for Present Perfect Continuous.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Integration of at least 8 health-related nouns, verbs, and adjectives (e.g., <b>well-being</b>, <b>tracker</b>, <b>mindfulness</b>, <b>improve</b>, <b>manage</b>, <b>balanced</b>, <b>energized</b>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and coherence of speech:</b> Correct and appropriate use of Present Perfect Continuous for ongoing habits, Second Conditional for hypothetical ideas, and Modals of possibility for suggestions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative interaction and pragmatic functions:</b> Taking turns, actively listening, showing <b>empathy</b>, and giving polite <b>suggestions</b> using an appropriate tone.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did I use the present perfect continuous and second conditional to discuss health habits and hypothetical improvements during the role-play?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I feel comfortable giving health suggestions politely and showing empathy when discussing well-being with my partner?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about discussing your personal health habits and aspirations using health technology language, and what strategies did you use to overcome these challenges?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can you apply the language and conversational strategies from today's lesson to talk about health and <b>well-being</b> outside the classroom, perhaps with family or friends?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The role-play activity (Stage 4) effectively engaged students in using the target grammar and vocabulary in a communicative context. Students demonstrated good understanding of the Present Perfect Continuous for ongoing actions and modals for suggestions. The pronunciation focus on /b/-/p/ and /s/-/z/ was generally successful, though some students still require more practice with sentence rhythm in PPC.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Some students struggled to consistently use the Second Conditional for hypothetical situations. For the next lesson, I will need to provide more explicit scaffolding or mini-drills focusing on this structure. I could also introduce more varied scenarios for giving suggestions to encourage the use of different modals.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The peer assessment aspect worked well for promoting active listening and self-correction. Overall, the lesson achieved its objective of practicing speaking about health habits and using technology for good habits.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 4 (Writing Composition), students will synthesize the ideas discussed about health technology and habits into a structured written piece. They will describe their ideal healthy <b>lifestyle</b> incorporating technology, drawing upon the vocabulary and grammar practiced in this speaking lesson to form coherent paragraphs and express their personal <b>dreams</b> and <b>ambitions</b> for <b>well-being</b>.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>